!                                                                             !
!                This CHEMKIN mechanism file is part of the                   !
!                        Supplemental Material for                            !
!                                                                             !
!          A detailed kinetic submechanism for OH* chemiluminescence          ! 
!              in hydrogen combustion revisited. Parts 1 and 2                !
!                                                                             !
!              Alexander S. Sharipov*1, Boris I. Loukhovitski**1,             !
!               Alexey V. Pelevkin***2, Mayya R. Korshunova****1              !
!                                                                             !
! 1 Joint Institute for High Temperatures of the Russian Academy of Sciences  !
! 2 Prokhorov General Physics Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences    !
!                                                                             !
!                  * aleksandr.sharipov@phystech.edu (theory)                 !
!                 ** boris.loukhovitski@yandex.ru    (modeling)               !
!                *** pelevkin@phystech.edu           (theory)                 !
!               **** korshunova@labnp-jiht.ru        (experimental)           !
!                                                                             !
!                       Combustion and Flame, 2024                            !
!                                                                             !
! Mechanism of this file comprises three parts:                               !
!  -  H2/O2 kinetic model of Varga et al. (2015)                              !
!  -  NOx reaction subset embedded in the CRECK chemistry model               !
!  -  OH* kinetics submechanism developed in this work "JIHT-OHex(H2)"        !
!                                                                             !
!  but the OH* kinetics we developed can be used together with any            !
!  other ground-state H2-O2-N2 chemistry model.                               !
!                                                                             !
